n. 0 means the SDK’s default (5);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it’s capped at the issuer’s batch size."}]},"doc://oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet/documentation/OID4VCWallet/WalletConfiguration/tlsPins":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/oid4vcwallet\/walletconfiguration\/tlspins","title":"tlsPins","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/WalletConfiguration\/tlsPins","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tlsPins","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pins hosts’ certificates for the wallet’s own HTTPS requests:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"host → base64 SHA-256 digests of a certificate’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SubjectPublicKeyInfo, one of which a certificate in the verified"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain must have, or the request fails as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tlsPin"},{"type":"text","text":" before anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent. A host is a name, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*."},{"type":"text","text":" and one, matching any name a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"label below it; not an IP address. Pins add to certificate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verification, never replace it: pin a CA’s key, so a leaf renewal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t break the app, and keep a backup pin. They cover the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests the SDK makes (issuers, Authorization Servers,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Verifiers, status lists), not the app’s own, such as to its"},{"type":"te